WEBVTT

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.240
-Stop!
-Dang!

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:37.820
-Get the cars!
-After them!

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:40.080
What are you doing?

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:41.580
Hurry up!

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:02.390
KEEP UP THE GOOD WORK!

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:10.360
There's five billion here
in non-sequential bills.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:13.030
Here's a shower of money! Take that!

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:14.860
Hot! Hot! Hot!

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:15.860
Steaming hot!

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:18.450
Bury me some more!

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:30.710
What's wrong, Lupin?

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:32.300
-Let's dump it.
-What!

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:34.510
These are counterfeit.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:35.840
Well-made, but still.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:37.340
They are?

00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:39.050
They can't be...

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:41.810
We swiped these from the vault
of a state-run casino.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:43.680
They're Gothic bills.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:44.850
Gothic bills?

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:46.680
Those legendary counterfeits?

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:50.110
So, they're even showing up
at state-run casinos now?

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.770
Jigen, that's it! That's our next job.

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:55.530
What do you say we party
hard to celebrate in advance?

00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:57.530
Party!

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:02.200
Damn it!

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:03.830
Stupid things! Damn it! Damn it!

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:04.990
Damn it!

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:19.630
LUPIN THE THIRD
THE CASTLE OF CAGLIOSTRO

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:42.110
I've never heard
of this Principality of Cagliostro.

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:44.360
Population, 3,500.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.860
It's the world's smallest state
to be a member of the UN.

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:49.870
And it's where the Gothic bills
are coming from, huh?

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:52.790
It's a famous legend
among those in the know.

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:54.540
The black hole
of the world of counterfeit bills.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:56.790
Black hole?

00:04:57.080 --> 00:05:00.130
The story goes that folks
who snoop around are never seen again.

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:02.880
Scary.

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:06.010
It's scary, so I'm going to sleep.

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:18.310
Hey.

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:36.040
What the heck? This spare is totally bald.

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:54.970
Talk about peaceful.

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:10.660
-What the...
-Get in!

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:33.600
-So, who do we side with?
-The woman!

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:34.640
Thought so!

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:44.770
-The tires!
-Got it!

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:08.920
Dang! That's no ordinary car!

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:21.020
Now, this is getting interesting!

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:22.270
We're taking the lead!

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:41.040
Took it!

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:45.840
The next shot won't be any ordinary slug.

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:57.010
Yes!

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:12.700
She's fainted.

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:21.370
That car's going to fall apart.

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:22.330
Take the wheel!

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:34.610
No, let me go!

00:09:34.690 --> 00:09:36.900
Hey! No! No, no! Watch it!
Down! Down! Down! Look down!

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:38.820
Look down, I said! Look down!

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:45.870
Good, that's it. Hold it right there.

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:18.320
Hello?

00:10:19.070 --> 00:10:19.910
Sir?

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:39.260
Sir? Sir?

00:10:45.770 --> 00:10:46.810
I'm sorry.

00:11:05.530 --> 00:11:06.370
Hey!

00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:07.830
Yo, Lupin.

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:10.080
Man, you're one sorry mess.

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:11.580
Where'd my bride go?

00:11:14.710 --> 00:11:15.960
Dear, oh, dear.

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:22.550
Damn it!

00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:25.180
All that for one measly girl?
Who the heck were they?

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:33.690
It's a ring.

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:35.650
Hold on, I've seen this somewhere bef--

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:47.280
What's gotten into you?

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:49.250
You suddenly got all weird
after seeing the ring!

00:12:20.190 --> 00:12:22.950
Hey, Lupin, is there something
at this old castle?

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:31.950
It's the same crest as
the one on the ring...

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:32.960
Lupin.

00:12:45.050 --> 00:12:47.760
It hasn't been too long
since this place was abandoned.

00:12:50.760 --> 00:12:51.770
A fire...

00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:52.680
Who's there?

00:12:52.770 --> 00:12:54.310
Just passing through.

00:12:54.390 --> 00:12:55.390
Tourists?

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:56.560
Well, yeah.

00:12:56.690 --> 00:13:00.900
I thought this was supposed to be
His Highness, the Prince's palace.

00:13:01.110 --> 00:13:02.320
It still is.

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:05.030
This place isn't for outsiders
to just come poking around.

00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:07.240
You say this is the Prince's palace?

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:08.780
But it's an empty ruin.

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:12.660
Because of the big fire seven years ago.

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:15.620
Ever since the Prince
and his wife passed away,

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:18.330
it's been left to fall apart,
as you can see.

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:21.630
That's odd.
The Prince is basically the king, right?

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:23.260
So, there's no king now?

00:13:23.920 --> 00:13:26.970
There's a regent,
so it's apparently not a problem.

00:13:27.340 --> 00:13:28.510
Don't linger, you hear?

00:13:29.090 --> 00:13:30.100
Yeah, sure.

00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:33.220
Hey, Lupin.

00:14:55.260 --> 00:14:56.930
You went and got all grown up...

00:15:25.920 --> 00:15:27.050
What's up?

00:15:27.130 --> 00:15:28.710
Don't play dumb.

00:15:30.590 --> 00:15:31.970
Quit acting cool and keeping your problems
to yourself! Out with it!

00:15:32.050 --> 00:15:33.340
No, no, no, no! You're choking me!

00:15:33.430 --> 00:15:35.760
No! No!

00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:39.770
Talk! You gonna talk?

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:40.980
I'll talk, I'll talk,
I'll talk, I'll talk...

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:08.670
That's the castle of the regent,
the Count of Cagliostro.

00:16:09.090 --> 00:16:10.300
Look there.

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:12.130
Lower.

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:15.970
On the other side of the aqueduct.

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:19.770
It's that boat from earlier!

00:16:20.430 --> 00:16:22.390
So, the bride is inside that castle.

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:25.690
There's a sluice gate there.
It's exactly the same as it was back then.

00:16:26.190 --> 00:16:28.690
You've snuck into that castle before?

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:32.030
It was over 10 years ago.

00:16:32.530 --> 00:16:35.200
I was gonna solve the mystery
of the Gothic bills.

00:16:35.280 --> 00:16:37.070
I was just a punk,
still wet behind the ears.

00:16:37.490 --> 00:16:38.620
And? How'd it go?

00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:41.000
I got my butt kicked.

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:43.710
Turned tail and got out of there.

00:16:57.300 --> 00:16:59.220
An autogyro? Talk about old-fashioned.

00:16:59.300 --> 00:17:00.470
That's the Count.

00:17:00.930 --> 00:17:02.560
Come on, let's go look
for an inn or something.

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:04.310
Hey... Hey!

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:32.710
Jodot, that was careless.

00:17:32.800 --> 00:17:34.300
My apologies, sir.

00:17:34.380 --> 00:17:37.050
She was at a fitting
for her wedding attire

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:39.850
and the men were not present at the time.

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:42.850
She's in the north tower now?

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:46.560
Yes, sir. The drugs have put her
into a sound sleep.

00:17:51.690 --> 00:17:52.900
Foreigners...

00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:54.150
Yes, sir.

00:17:54.230 --> 00:17:58.200
I am told that a pair of men
aided her during her escape.

00:17:59.990 --> 00:18:02.910
Find them. Dispose of them how you will.

00:19:12.190 --> 00:19:13.360
The ring is gone!

00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:32.170
Get me Jodot!

00:19:54.230 --> 00:19:56.980
These letters are from the Gothic alphabet
that no one uses anymore.

00:19:57.070 --> 00:19:58.230
The Gothic alphabet?

00:19:58.320 --> 00:20:01.990
"With light and shadow as one once more,
it shall surely be restored.

00:20:02.070 --> 00:20:03.740
1517."

00:20:04.110 --> 00:20:05.910
The year is in Roman numerals.

00:20:05.990 --> 00:20:07.700
So, this thing's 400 years old.

00:20:07.990 --> 00:20:10.370
-Sorry for the wait!
-Looks tasty.

00:20:10.450 --> 00:20:12.710
You seem awfully preoccupied.
What are you looking at?

00:20:12.830 --> 00:20:16.790
I picked up this old ring
and I was wondering if it's valuable.

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:18.500
Oh, my! It's pretty!

00:20:18.590 --> 00:20:20.460
This is the Lady Clarisse's crest.

00:20:20.550 --> 00:20:21.630
Clarisse...

00:20:21.970 --> 00:20:23.300
Look, that's her.

00:20:23.380 --> 00:20:24.590
That photo up there.

00:20:25.550 --> 00:20:27.390
That's of when she was little, though.

00:20:28.140 --> 00:20:30.140
She returned from the convent yesterday.

00:20:30.560 --> 00:20:32.270
I imagine she's grown
into a fine young lady.

00:20:32.350 --> 00:20:33.390
The convent?

00:20:33.520 --> 00:20:34.900
You don't know?

00:20:34.980 --> 00:20:36.100
I thought you'd come to see

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:39.480
the Lady Clarisse
and the Count's wedding, too.

00:20:39.570 --> 00:20:40.480
So that's it!

00:20:40.570 --> 00:20:43.450
I was thinking there
were a lot of tourists here.

00:20:43.780 --> 00:20:45.570
But I feel sorry for the Lady Clarisse.

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:48.330
The Count is a notorious
womanizer, you know.

00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:50.540
Oh, my! Just like me!

00:20:50.620 --> 00:20:52.290
How does tonight sound?

00:20:52.580 --> 00:20:55.120
-Oh, please!
-Well? Well?

00:20:59.340 --> 00:21:01.460
A spy for the Count, just like we thought.

00:21:01.550 --> 00:21:04.220
His expression changed the moment
he saw the ring.

00:21:04.300 --> 00:21:05.760
Isn't the bride enough by herself?

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:07.260
He wants the ring, too!

00:21:07.430 --> 00:21:09.890
Not if I can help it!

00:21:10.970 --> 00:21:13.930
You knew that girl we saw today
was the Princess, didn't you?

00:21:14.940 --> 00:21:16.690
Didn't I clue you in?

00:21:31.030 --> 00:21:34.910
"With light and shadow as one once
more, it shall surely be restored," huh?

00:21:38.290 --> 00:21:40.790
You think it'll be
some treasure that's restored?

00:22:13.700 --> 00:22:15.000
Why you!

00:22:20.960 --> 00:22:23.170
Wow, here comes
the whole kit and caboodle!

00:22:24.670 --> 00:22:25.670
You creep!

00:22:37.270 --> 00:22:38.640
The Magnum doesn't work on them!

00:22:38.770 --> 00:22:40.600
These guys are professional assassins.

00:22:58.000 --> 00:22:59.000
Hurry!

00:23:11.300 --> 00:23:14.890
-That sure got my blood pumping.
-That was a full-blown attack.

00:23:14.970 --> 00:23:16.560
This is one deep rabbit hole!

00:23:16.640 --> 00:23:18.140
Yeah, this is getting interesting.

00:23:53.720 --> 00:23:55.220
These didn't turn out well.

00:23:55.720 --> 00:23:58.180
The quality has been
on a downward spiral lately.

00:23:58.770 --> 00:24:00.060
My apologies, sir.

00:24:00.140 --> 00:24:03.350
But if we continue to mass-produce
at our current pace...

00:24:04.100 --> 00:24:05.230
Redo these.

00:24:05.310 --> 00:24:07.020
And don't let
the delivery date slip, either.

00:24:07.150 --> 00:24:08.150
Yes, sir.

00:24:08.320 --> 00:24:09.360
Who's there?

00:24:13.610 --> 00:24:15.820
I, Jodot, have never blundered so greatly.

00:24:15.910 --> 00:24:17.780
The rats got away.

00:24:21.330 --> 00:24:23.750
Jodot, what's that piece of paper
on your back?

00:24:26.420 --> 00:24:27.380
This is...

00:24:27.500 --> 00:24:28.420
LUPIN IS ON THE SCENE

00:24:28.500 --> 00:24:29.670
When did that get there?

00:24:29.880 --> 00:24:30.920
Lupin...

00:24:31.010 --> 00:24:32.550
It is an advance notice from Lupin.

00:24:33.260 --> 00:24:34.090
Read it.

00:24:34.180 --> 00:24:36.090
Yes, sir. But...

00:24:36.680 --> 00:24:37.680
It's fine.

00:24:40.020 --> 00:24:43.560
"To the Count of lust and greed,
I will be taking your bride.

00:24:43.940 --> 00:24:46.810
Expect me soon. Lupin the Third."

00:24:48.610 --> 00:24:50.070
You should be happy about this, Jodot.

00:24:50.150 --> 00:24:50.980
Sir?

00:24:52.570 --> 00:24:53.900
Let us wait then.

00:24:54.240 --> 00:24:55.990
For this Lupin to come.

00:25:35.030 --> 00:25:37.530
UDON NOODLES WITH DEEP FRIED TOFU

00:25:39.780 --> 00:25:41.620
Hey, you got here fast.

00:25:43.910 --> 00:25:44.870
A job?

00:25:50.790 --> 00:25:51.880
Goemon's here.

00:25:51.960 --> 00:25:53.550
They're here, too.

00:25:53.920 --> 00:25:54.840
Take a peek.

00:26:01.640 --> 00:26:02.970
That's a Japanese police car!

00:26:03.060 --> 00:26:04.680
-It's Zenigata.
-What?

00:26:05.180 --> 00:26:06.940
SAITAMA

00:26:07.140 --> 00:26:08.850
All personnel, disembark!

00:26:09.900 --> 00:26:11.230
Fall in!

00:26:14.900 --> 00:26:17.280
And now, the cast is complete.

00:26:27.330 --> 00:26:29.670
Pardon me for interrupting your meal.

00:26:35.210 --> 00:26:37.130
I am Zenigata of the International
Criminal Police Organization.

00:26:37.630 --> 00:26:40.050
It was reported that you received
an advance notice from Lupin

00:26:40.140 --> 00:26:41.340
and that is why I am here.

00:26:43.140 --> 00:26:45.140
You mean that petty thief

00:26:45.220 --> 00:26:47.730
who's the third-generation
Arsène Lupin or whatever?

00:26:47.810 --> 00:26:51.900
Is Interpol in the habit of disturbing
people's breakfasts for such things?

00:26:51.980 --> 00:26:54.480
Your Excellency,
Lupin is not to be underestimated.

00:26:54.570 --> 00:26:56.530
If he says he'll come,
he will, without fail.

00:26:56.610 --> 00:26:58.070
There are five days until your nuptials.

00:26:58.570 --> 00:27:01.610
I insist that you allow us
to patrol your castle.

00:27:04.580 --> 00:27:06.700
We have police in this country,
too, you know.

00:27:06.790 --> 00:27:10.000
Though, we refer to them
more elegantly as gendarmes.

00:27:10.870 --> 00:27:11.960
You called, sir?

00:27:12.460 --> 00:27:15.960
Gustav, cooperate with this Japanese man.

00:27:16.050 --> 00:27:17.090
You're dismissed.

00:27:17.380 --> 00:27:19.590
Yes, sir! One more thing, Your Excellency.

00:27:19.670 --> 00:27:22.550
Please tell me why that scoundrel Lupin
would be after your bride.

00:27:23.220 --> 00:27:24.350
Who knows?

00:27:24.640 --> 00:27:27.560
Isn't investigating that part
of your job as well?

00:27:28.560 --> 00:27:29.850
Please excuse me.

00:27:33.860 --> 00:27:35.270
Are you sure about this, sir?

00:27:35.360 --> 00:27:37.730
Allowing such a man
inside the castle would be...

00:27:37.820 --> 00:27:41.320
I don't care.
I have lots of friends at Interpol, too.

00:27:41.400 --> 00:27:43.410
I'm sure he'll have
to withdraw in no time.

00:27:46.200 --> 00:27:49.080
There's Zenigata. Talk about a child
of the early Shōwa era.

00:27:49.160 --> 00:27:50.660
He is one hard worker.

00:28:01.300 --> 00:28:02.680
What is that?

00:28:03.220 --> 00:28:04.840
Don't go any farther.

00:28:05.350 --> 00:28:06.350
What?

00:28:06.890 --> 00:28:07.970
Watch.

00:28:12.520 --> 00:28:15.150
If you don't want to die,
don't go wandering around.

00:28:15.310 --> 00:28:16.940
You let your men know that, too.

00:28:22.110 --> 00:28:24.780
Inspector, we've detected
an antipersonnel radar as well.

00:28:25.530 --> 00:28:26.990
I don't like this castle.

00:28:27.080 --> 00:28:29.700
They've got too many preventative
measures for amateurs.

00:28:32.960 --> 00:28:33.960
A woman?

00:28:34.370 --> 00:28:36.460
Hold on now, don't say you're out.

00:28:36.540 --> 00:28:39.090
There's a woman mixed up in this,
but that's not the whole story.

00:28:39.170 --> 00:28:41.510
Is there something
special about this ring?

00:28:42.130 --> 00:28:44.550
Once we get the girl back
from the dirty old Count,

00:28:44.630 --> 00:28:46.220
we'll know that, too.

00:28:46.590 --> 00:28:49.930
After all, these are monsters
that the Magnum can't touch.

00:28:50.010 --> 00:28:52.980
Between your blade
and this anti-tank rifle...

00:28:54.310 --> 00:28:55.980
Hey, Lupin, figured out how to get in yet?

00:28:56.060 --> 00:28:56.980
Nope.

00:28:57.110 --> 00:29:00.110
The place is incredible.
It's a nest full of lasers and radars.

00:29:00.900 --> 00:29:02.110
I see.

00:29:02.190 --> 00:29:03.610
We'll need a tank then...

00:29:03.700 --> 00:29:05.530
So you called Zenigata.

00:29:05.610 --> 00:29:07.160
What? Is that true, Lupin?

00:29:07.240 --> 00:29:10.580
Bingo! You've got good instincts.

00:29:11.330 --> 00:29:13.870
So, you will fight fire with fire.

00:29:19.290 --> 00:29:21.090
This is the Castle of Cagliostro.

00:29:21.170 --> 00:29:22.460
We're here.

00:29:22.550 --> 00:29:24.670
This Roman aqueduct is still in use today.

00:29:25.220 --> 00:29:27.010
This is our only way in.

00:29:27.890 --> 00:29:31.930
They use the Roman aqueduct
to draw water to the castle from the lake.

00:29:32.560 --> 00:29:33.770
I see.

00:29:33.850 --> 00:29:36.600
And there won't be any lasers underwater.

00:29:37.600 --> 00:29:39.270
Goemon, you're the lookout.

00:29:46.990 --> 00:29:48.570
Watch out. There's a hole there.

00:30:00.500 --> 00:30:01.840
Our first obstacle, huh?

00:30:04.010 --> 00:30:05.010
Here we go.

00:31:05.480 --> 00:31:07.490
Lupin!

00:31:26.420 --> 00:31:29.050
That's the machine room
of the clock tower.

00:31:29.840 --> 00:31:31.550
I wonder if that son-of-a-gun
made it all right.

00:31:59.450 --> 00:32:00.910
What's that windmill?

00:32:01.250 --> 00:32:04.380
According to Gustav,
it brings water up into the castle, sir.

00:32:06.960 --> 00:32:08.340
Where does that water come out?

00:32:08.420 --> 00:32:09.840
A fountain in the battery up above, sir.

00:32:09.920 --> 00:32:10.800
-Come with me!
-Yes, sir!

00:32:37.280 --> 00:32:39.700
Inspector! Paris Headquarters
has ordered our withdrawal.

00:32:39.790 --> 00:32:41.080
We are to return at once.

00:32:41.660 --> 00:32:44.710
What preposterous nonsense is this?
I'm verifying this!

00:32:58.930 --> 00:33:00.770
What did you say?
Lupin's advance notice...

00:33:00.850 --> 00:33:02.230
So, the justification was...

00:33:03.230 --> 00:33:04.350
The Count?

00:33:05.440 --> 00:33:07.400
Police officers are
not boot-licking lackeys!

00:33:07.480 --> 00:33:09.360
Whether he likes it or not...

00:33:09.940 --> 00:33:11.650
Hello? Hello!

00:33:12.030 --> 00:33:13.860
Dammit...

00:33:14.400 --> 00:33:16.030
I'm taking this up with the Count!

00:33:19.950 --> 00:33:22.750
And there's your personal guide
to the Count.

00:33:27.130 --> 00:33:28.920
I want to see the Count immediately.

00:33:29.170 --> 00:33:31.000
Did you hear me? Let me through!

00:33:31.090 --> 00:33:32.300
Give it up.

00:33:33.630 --> 00:33:36.550
Only those deemed trustworthy
are permitted beyond this point.

00:33:37.430 --> 00:33:40.050
What? Are you saying that
the ICPO can't be trusted?

00:33:40.560 --> 00:33:43.100
I believe you have
been ordered to withdraw.

00:33:43.180 --> 00:33:44.060
Please take your leave.

00:33:45.640 --> 00:33:47.400
How did you know about that?

00:33:47.600 --> 00:33:50.440
We can deal with the likes of Lupin
without the help of you Orientals.

00:33:50.520 --> 00:33:51.400
Now, leave.

00:33:54.610 --> 00:33:56.070
I see. I understand.

00:33:56.150 --> 00:33:57.360
We'll pull out for now.

00:33:57.450 --> 00:33:58.320
Yes, sir.

00:34:10.590 --> 00:34:12.710
-Did you just see me come here?
-What?

00:34:12.800 --> 00:34:14.460
You blithering idiot! That was Lupin!

00:34:14.550 --> 00:34:16.050
He disguised himself as me and got inside!

00:34:16.300 --> 00:34:18.680
All that brawn and you can't
even see through a disguise?

00:34:18.760 --> 00:34:20.550
-You good-for-nothing!
-Darn it!

00:34:20.640 --> 00:34:21.970
Follow me!

00:34:23.140 --> 00:34:25.270
Don't let Lupin get away!

00:34:31.690 --> 00:34:32.690
Stop right there!

00:34:34.400 --> 00:34:35.400
Lupin!

00:34:35.820 --> 00:34:36.690
Lupin?

00:34:38.700 --> 00:34:41.160
Stop this! Lupin is... Lupin is...

00:34:41.780 --> 00:34:42.950
Help the Chief Inspector!

00:34:43.030 --> 00:34:44.490
Attack!

00:34:51.080 --> 00:34:52.920
Wow, look at them going at it!

00:34:54.500 --> 00:34:56.420
Stop it! That's Lupin!

00:34:56.510 --> 00:34:57.970
Darn it!

00:34:59.300 --> 00:35:00.260
Get off my foot!

00:35:16.190 --> 00:35:17.440
Lupin!

00:35:33.670 --> 00:35:35.290
It seems we caught something.

00:35:41.180 --> 00:35:43.720
The idiot. He should have
gotten himself out of here.

00:35:43.800 --> 00:35:44.800
The gendarmes are gone, sir.

00:35:44.890 --> 00:35:45.930
Gustav!

00:35:46.010 --> 00:35:47.470
Leaving his post?

00:35:47.560 --> 00:35:48.770
What is he doing?

00:35:49.770 --> 00:35:50.890
You stay here.

00:35:50.980 --> 00:35:51.850
Yes, sir.

00:35:53.980 --> 00:35:55.400
Sorry, Pops.

00:35:57.570 --> 00:36:00.440
You fool! Call off this insanity at once!

00:36:00.530 --> 00:36:01.700
Do you not see?

00:36:01.780 --> 00:36:04.120
You fell for Lupin's ruse,
hook, line, and sinker!

00:36:04.200 --> 00:36:05.700
Darn it!

00:36:10.370 --> 00:36:12.460
Hey! Let go! Let go!

00:36:19.880 --> 00:36:22.300
So, that Lupin finally made his way in.

00:36:22.380 --> 00:36:24.140
I have no words to express my shame.

00:36:25.010 --> 00:36:28.100
Tell the police force that
their inspector went ahead and left.

00:36:28.560 --> 00:36:31.140
Mysterious disappearances
en route happen all the time.

00:36:31.230 --> 00:36:32.060
Yes, sir.

00:36:55.750 --> 00:36:57.290
Don't move.

00:36:59.500 --> 00:37:01.210
Good evening, Fujicakes.

00:37:01.300 --> 00:37:02.130
Lupin!

00:37:02.220 --> 00:37:05.380
A woman engrossed in her work
is a beautiful sight.

00:37:05.470 --> 00:37:07.350
You've gotten this far inside already?

00:37:07.640 --> 00:37:10.560
We haven't seen each other
in a year and that's all I get?

00:37:10.640 --> 00:37:11.770
I searched high and low, you know.

00:37:12.560 --> 00:37:13.560
Lupin...

00:37:13.640 --> 00:37:16.150
What you're searching for
is where the bride is, right?

00:37:16.560 --> 00:37:18.230
Oh, you knew?

00:37:18.560 --> 00:37:21.860
I don't mind telling you, but promise
you won't get in the way of my work?

00:37:22.110 --> 00:37:24.360
I won't, I won't! I never have!

00:37:24.650 --> 00:37:25.780
I don't know about that.

00:37:26.240 --> 00:37:28.030
The top of the tower on the north side.

00:37:28.120 --> 00:37:30.870
Though, I imagine it'll be
impossible for you to get in.

00:37:35.000 --> 00:37:36.080
Lupin...

00:38:01.730 --> 00:38:04.690
Dang. What an awful place
to lock someone up.

00:39:23.440 --> 00:39:24.940
Oh, no, no, no, no, no!

00:39:36.240 --> 00:39:37.870
Got i-- Wha?

00:41:03.120 --> 00:41:04.120
Who are you?

00:41:04.710 --> 00:41:06.210
I am a thief.

00:41:07.250 --> 00:41:08.460
A thief, sir?

00:41:13.010 --> 00:41:14.930
Good evening, Miss Bride.

00:41:16.430 --> 00:41:18.510
You are that man from earlier, aren't you?

00:41:18.600 --> 00:41:19.890
You forgot this.

00:41:23.060 --> 00:41:24.140
My!

00:41:24.230 --> 00:41:25.770
You came all this way just for this?

00:41:25.850 --> 00:41:27.940
When you would be killed
if the Count were to find you?

00:41:28.270 --> 00:41:32.320
But it is in the nature of a thief
to target and be targeted.

00:41:32.400 --> 00:41:34.320
I will leave once the job is done.

00:41:34.990 --> 00:41:36.030
The job?

00:41:37.570 --> 00:41:40.700
If only there were something
I could offer you, but...

00:41:41.370 --> 00:41:42.750
I am a captive right now.

00:41:45.370 --> 00:41:46.420
Take this.

00:41:50.170 --> 00:41:51.380
My target is a treasure

00:41:51.460 --> 00:41:55.590
that an evil sorcerer locked away
at the top of a tall tower.

00:41:59.470 --> 00:42:02.720
Please allow yourself
to be stolen away by this thief.

00:42:03.350 --> 00:42:04.430
Me?

00:42:08.150 --> 00:42:11.070
Rescuing jewels held prisoner in safes...

00:42:11.820 --> 00:42:15.030
And releasing girls
about to be forced into marriage

00:42:15.110 --> 00:42:17.530
to run free in green fields...

00:42:19.030 --> 00:42:22.160
These are all jobs for a thief.

00:42:23.120 --> 00:42:24.830
You would give me my freedom?

00:42:40.220 --> 00:42:41.220
Thank you.

00:42:41.300 --> 00:42:42.430
I really appreciate it.

00:42:43.430 --> 00:42:47.060
But you do not know just how terrible
the House of Cagliostro is.

00:42:50.150 --> 00:42:51.940
Please, just leave.

00:42:59.360 --> 00:43:01.870
Oh, how could this be?

00:43:01.950 --> 00:43:05.370
The girl believes in
the evil sorcerer's powers,

00:43:05.450 --> 00:43:07.960
and yet, she would not try
to believe in the thief's powers.

00:43:08.330 --> 00:43:10.120
If the girl would only believe,

00:43:10.620 --> 00:43:12.750
the thief would be
capable of flying the skies

00:43:12.840 --> 00:43:16.510
or even drinking the lake dry!

00:43:40.780 --> 00:43:41.820
My!

00:43:42.570 --> 00:43:44.830
Right now, this is the best he can do.

00:44:19.490 --> 00:44:20.780
Sir thief!

00:44:21.610 --> 00:44:24.660
Hey! Treat the lady with more respect!

00:44:35.330 --> 00:44:38.920
Thank you for coming all this way
to deliver the ring, my dear Lupin.

00:44:39.050 --> 00:44:42.050
I'm deeply touched by
the grand welcome, Count.

00:44:42.550 --> 00:44:45.050
I hate to get right to it, but I'm
going to have you go away now.

00:44:45.390 --> 00:44:47.970
Oh, but will you be able
to get rid of me so easily?

00:44:48.850 --> 00:44:51.270
No! You must not injure that man!

00:44:51.350 --> 00:44:54.600
It'll be OK, missy. You have to have faith
in the thief's powers.

00:44:57.020 --> 00:44:58.110
Monsieur!

00:44:58.440 --> 00:45:01.070
Yes! The Monsieur is here!

00:45:01.150 --> 00:45:02.950
He'll be right back, OK?

00:45:04.860 --> 00:45:06.660
Now, what's the game going to be?

00:45:07.200 --> 00:45:09.450
It would be easy to tear you apart,

00:45:09.540 --> 00:45:12.000
but I hardly think we need
to sully the bride's room

00:45:12.080 --> 00:45:13.330
with the blood of a petty thief.

00:45:13.620 --> 00:45:15.420
You say that now...

00:45:15.500 --> 00:45:16.830
You'll regret it later.

00:45:17.540 --> 00:45:19.750
That will be the last
of your smart retorts.

00:45:27.220 --> 00:45:31.390
That hole leads to a hell that
no one has ever crawled out of.

00:46:01.750 --> 00:46:05.300
You look so sweet, and yet, you've
already attracted a man to your side.

00:46:05.380 --> 00:46:07.550
The Cagliostro blood always comes through.

00:46:09.550 --> 00:46:11.220
You are worthy of becoming my wife.

00:46:11.680 --> 00:46:13.970
Murderer. You are not human.

00:46:14.480 --> 00:46:17.640
Why, yes, my hands are covered in blood.

00:46:17.940 --> 00:46:19.650
But so are yours.

00:46:20.190 --> 00:46:21.520
Generation after generation,

00:46:21.610 --> 00:46:24.280
my family has served
as the shadow to your family,

00:46:24.360 --> 00:46:27.990
overseeing schemes and assassinations
to support this country.

00:46:28.070 --> 00:46:29.910
Let go of me! You disgust me!

00:46:32.990 --> 00:46:34.950
I won't have you telling me
that you didn't know.

00:46:36.160 --> 00:46:38.870
You are of Cagliostro as well.

00:46:38.960 --> 00:46:43.340
The same ancient blood of the Goths
that flows in my veins flows in yours.

00:46:46.470 --> 00:46:49.640
Clarisse, after four hundred long years,

00:46:49.720 --> 00:46:53.220
light and shadow, the two houses
of Cagliostro that have been divided,

00:46:53.310 --> 00:46:55.810
are now about to become as one.

00:46:56.350 --> 00:46:57.480
Take a look.

00:46:57.980 --> 00:47:00.730
This is the gold goat
that has been passed down in my family.

00:47:00.810 --> 00:47:01.770
When your...

00:47:02.690 --> 00:47:06.030
ring with the silver goat comes together
to become one with it,

00:47:06.110 --> 00:47:08.820
the hidden treasure of our ancestors
will be restored.

00:47:08.900 --> 00:47:11.030
<i>I heard that! I totally heard that!</i>

00:47:11.110 --> 00:47:13.120
<i>A marriage for treasure!</i>

00:47:13.200 --> 00:47:15.160
-It's him!
-<i>The counterfeit bill printer Count!</i>

00:47:15.240 --> 00:47:18.210
<i>Everything he says and does</i>
<i>are all a sham!</i>

00:47:18.290 --> 00:47:21.250
<i>The girl is a very kindhearted,</i>
<i>wonderful young lady.</i>

00:47:23.540 --> 00:47:24.500
Monsieur? Monsieur?

00:47:24.920 --> 00:47:26.590
<i>Yes! He's alive and well!</i>

00:47:26.800 --> 00:47:30.130
Thanks to the girl believing in him,
he can even fly the skies.

00:47:30.510 --> 00:47:32.800
Sir Thief will come
and steal you away for sure.

00:47:32.890 --> 00:47:34.720
-<i>So, you just wait.</i>
-I will.

00:47:35.350 --> 00:47:37.180
<i>Blast it! So it's that ring?</i>

00:47:37.640 --> 00:47:38.850
Give it here!

00:47:40.890 --> 00:47:42.770
<i>Hey, Count,</i>
<i>you listen and you listen good!</i>

00:47:44.060 --> 00:47:45.820
<i>I've got the real ring!</i>

00:47:45.900 --> 00:47:47.530
<i>You try and lay a finger on that girl,</i>

00:47:47.610 --> 00:47:49.900
<i>and here's what I'll do</i>
<i>to your precious ring!</i>

00:47:52.200 --> 00:47:53.200
It was a fake!

00:48:04.630 --> 00:48:05.960
Well, crap!

00:48:06.040 --> 00:48:09.380
Treat me like bodily wastes, will you?
Well, pooh-pooh to that!

00:48:10.220 --> 00:48:12.220
-Did he fall?
-Probably. Make sure.

00:48:12.300 --> 00:48:15.260
That is not a place fit
for the living to visit.

00:48:15.350 --> 00:48:17.430
He is certain to die
if we leave him down there.

00:48:17.510 --> 00:48:19.470
The weasel has the ring.

00:48:20.020 --> 00:48:21.270
As you wish, sir.

00:48:21.940 --> 00:48:23.020
You just wait!

00:48:23.100 --> 00:48:25.810
I'll tear that petty thief of yours
to shreds!

00:49:42.430 --> 00:49:45.310
Four hundred years
of killing and more killing...

00:49:45.390 --> 00:49:47.520
May you rest in peace.

00:49:51.690 --> 00:49:55.700
1904 3 14 JAPANESE ARMY SCOUT GENNOSUKE
KAWAKAMI PERISHED HERE. AVENGE...

00:50:12.590 --> 00:50:13.590
Lupin!

00:50:14.300 --> 00:50:16.470
Why you! Surrender quietly!

00:50:16.880 --> 00:50:18.720
Pops, I'm amazed you're all right.

00:50:18.800 --> 00:50:21.510
Tell me! Where's the exit?
Where'd you come in from?

00:50:21.600 --> 00:50:23.430
I got the shaft, too.

00:50:23.520 --> 00:50:24.350
What?

00:50:27.100 --> 00:50:29.270
By the looks of it, you've
been walking for quite a while.

00:50:29.810 --> 00:50:32.230
Shut up! I won't take pity from a thief!

00:50:32.820 --> 00:50:36.070
Well, let's kick back and relax.
There's no way out anyway.

00:50:37.360 --> 00:50:38.990
Make a little room for me there, will you?

00:50:40.660 --> 00:50:43.030
Pops, mind lending me a light?

00:50:43.120 --> 00:50:45.830
Lupin, what in the world is the deal
with this horde of dead bodies?

00:50:45.910 --> 00:50:47.160
It doesn't strike me as a gravesite.

00:50:47.790 --> 00:50:49.620
Take a look at the wall there.

00:50:57.130 --> 00:50:58.720
This is...

00:51:01.260 --> 00:51:03.220
May you rest in peace.

00:51:05.350 --> 00:51:07.480
I'd figured this was no ordinary castle,

00:51:07.560 --> 00:51:10.400
but a secret worth
going this far to keep...

00:51:10.480 --> 00:51:12.230
Is that what you're after, too?

00:51:12.980 --> 00:51:14.690
The one who's up to that is Fujicakes.

00:51:14.780 --> 00:51:17.240
I just hope she doesn't end up
joining the dearly departed.

00:51:17.990 --> 00:51:20.320
Anyway, making a fuss isn't going
to get us anywhere.

00:51:20.410 --> 00:51:22.740
Good night, Pops.

00:51:37.170 --> 00:51:38.510
Man, it's cold.

00:51:38.920 --> 00:51:42.180
Wow, look at the time. How do things look?

00:51:42.260 --> 00:51:43.350
No movement yet.

00:51:45.510 --> 00:51:47.270
Guess we'll just have to wait.

00:52:44.740 --> 00:52:45.570
Take that!

00:53:25.410 --> 00:53:26.280
They're taking too long.

00:53:28.120 --> 00:53:28.990
Master Jodot!

00:53:32.500 --> 00:53:33.830
Well done!

00:53:38.380 --> 00:53:39.630
And, heave!

00:53:43.420 --> 00:53:44.970
Curse you, Lupin!

00:53:52.430 --> 00:53:53.850
This is a coffin!

00:53:56.390 --> 00:53:57.730
What?

00:54:04.190 --> 00:54:05.610
What the heck is this place?

00:54:17.790 --> 00:54:19.210
These are 10,000-yen bills!

00:54:19.790 --> 00:54:21.710
Goodness! And so are all these?

00:54:24.050 --> 00:54:26.130
These are sure well-made.

00:54:26.380 --> 00:54:27.930
Pops, take a look.

00:54:29.300 --> 00:54:30.970
West German 1000-mark bills!

00:54:31.050 --> 00:54:32.810
Pounds. Dollars.

00:54:32.890 --> 00:54:36.270
Francs! Rubles! Rupees!
Pesos! Crowns! Liras!

00:54:36.980 --> 00:54:38.810
There's even won!

00:54:39.270 --> 00:54:40.610
They've got the whole world covered.

00:54:42.400 --> 00:54:44.570
Printing counterfeit bills!

00:54:44.650 --> 00:54:46.700
Lupin, so this is the castle's secret?

00:54:47.360 --> 00:54:48.200
That's right.

00:54:48.280 --> 00:54:51.160
Gothic bills were once hailed
as being superior to even the real thing

00:54:51.240 --> 00:54:52.530
and this is the heart of it all.

00:54:53.620 --> 00:54:55.620
<i>Fake currency has played a shadowy part</i>

00:54:55.700 --> 00:54:58.620
<i>in every upheaval in Europe</i>
<i>since the Middle Ages.</i>

00:54:58.710 --> 00:55:00.540
<i>It brought down the Bourbon Dynasty</i>

00:55:00.630 --> 00:55:02.750
<i>by serving as a source</i>
<i>of funds for Napoleon.</i>

00:55:03.210 --> 00:55:07.590
<i>And in 1927,</i>
<i>it also triggered the Great Depression.</i>

00:55:08.510 --> 00:55:12.050
<i>The key player of the black hole behind</i>
<i>the scenes of history, the Gothic bill.</i>

00:55:12.720 --> 00:55:14.810
<i>And of those who tried</i>
<i>to get a peek at its source,</i>

00:55:14.890 --> 00:55:16.810
<i>not a soul ever made it back out.</i>

00:55:19.640 --> 00:55:21.600
I'd heard the rumors,

00:55:21.690 --> 00:55:24.320
but I never imagined that
a sovereign nation was behind it.

00:55:25.190 --> 00:55:26.360
What'll you do, Pops?

00:55:26.440 --> 00:55:28.740
Now that you've seen it,
there's no going back.

00:55:29.240 --> 00:55:31.700
I know that. The police officer in me
is itching to get on the case.

00:55:33.070 --> 00:55:35.660
Temporary truce until we get out of here?

00:55:36.200 --> 00:55:39.210
Fine. But I won't aid a thief.

00:55:39.290 --> 00:55:42.130
Once we've escaped,
I'll arrest you without fail.

00:55:42.710 --> 00:55:44.880
Fantastic. OK, then...

00:55:44.960 --> 00:55:46.300
Let's shake on it!

00:55:48.340 --> 00:55:49.670
I won't collude with you.

00:55:49.760 --> 00:55:50.760
Well, now.

00:55:58.520 --> 00:55:59.350
Miss Fujiko.

00:55:59.430 --> 00:56:01.900
I saw my opportunity,
so I've come to say goodbye.

00:56:03.980 --> 00:56:05.150
What in the world are you...

00:56:05.940 --> 00:56:08.490
Hired as the Lady Clarisse's
personal servant,

00:56:08.570 --> 00:56:10.860
the one and only woman
inside the castle...

00:56:10.950 --> 00:56:11.860
But the truth is,

00:56:12.360 --> 00:56:14.780
I'm a female spy who came to delve
into this castle's secrets.

00:56:15.530 --> 00:56:18.540
I was planning on sticking around
a little longer, but Lupin came, right?

00:56:18.620 --> 00:56:20.870
It's going to become messy,
so I'm leaving.

00:56:21.370 --> 00:56:23.210
You know that gentleman?

00:56:23.290 --> 00:56:24.750
Better than I wish I ever did.

00:56:25.590 --> 00:56:28.090
Allies at times and enemies at others.

00:56:28.170 --> 00:56:30.420
I suppose we might've been lovers
at one point, too.

00:56:30.970 --> 00:56:33.260
He's a born womanizer. Be careful.

00:56:34.010 --> 00:56:35.100
He left you?

00:56:35.390 --> 00:56:36.760
Certainly not.

00:56:36.850 --> 00:56:38.100
I left him.

00:56:42.270 --> 00:56:44.060
Smoke coming from the pitfall!

00:56:44.150 --> 00:56:45.150
A fire...

00:56:48.400 --> 00:56:49.860
It's coming from the basement.

00:56:52.740 --> 00:56:54.820
-Movement!
-So, he's kicked things off!

00:57:08.130 --> 00:57:10.420
Bad news, sir! The fire's origin
is believed to be the basement workshop!

00:57:10.960 --> 00:57:13.050
-What? Put it out right away!
-Yes, sir!

00:57:13.130 --> 00:57:14.380
Darn you! Shut that thing!

00:57:14.470 --> 00:57:15.430
You all go, too!

00:57:16.970 --> 00:57:18.970
Blasted Jodot. Don't tell me he failed...

00:57:25.060 --> 00:57:27.690
Pops, hurry it up!
We're going to have visitors soon!

00:57:27.900 --> 00:57:29.980
Proof! I need proof!

00:57:36.280 --> 00:57:37.780
Curse you, Lupin!

00:57:40.200 --> 00:57:42.950
Find him! He should still be in here!

00:57:46.710 --> 00:57:49.170
Don't let it scare you! Get to it!

00:57:54.630 --> 00:57:56.260
There's Lupin! After him!

00:57:56.340 --> 00:57:57.800
You put the fire out!

00:58:05.690 --> 00:58:06.770
It's the chapel!

00:58:13.440 --> 00:58:14.320
Monsieur!

00:58:14.400 --> 00:58:15.820
Lupin! And Zenigata, too?

00:58:23.410 --> 00:58:25.000
They mean to steal the autogyro.

00:58:28.960 --> 00:58:29.830
<i>You fool!</i>

00:58:29.920 --> 00:58:32.800
I will take my reprimand later.
He is going after the Lady Clarisse!

00:58:32.880 --> 00:58:33.800
Please hurry!

00:58:41.760 --> 00:58:42.970
Hurry up!

00:58:51.400 --> 00:58:53.320
Darn it! Don't underestimate
the Metropolitan Police!

00:58:53.400 --> 00:58:54.610
Pops, get on!

00:59:04.700 --> 00:59:06.200
So long!

00:59:06.290 --> 00:59:08.540
Pops, I'm going to make a quick pit stop.

00:59:08.620 --> 00:59:10.500
If this is a kidnapping for ransom,
I won't cooperate.

00:59:10.580 --> 00:59:11.710
It's a non-business venture.

00:59:18.550 --> 00:59:19.760
He's coming this way.

00:59:38.780 --> 00:59:39.820
It's bulletproof glass!

00:59:41.950 --> 00:59:44.080
We can't open this!
Please, don't mind me and just go!

00:59:54.460 --> 00:59:55.750
Pops, take the wheel.

00:59:55.840 --> 00:59:58.970
What? Wait, Lupin, I've never done this!

00:59:59.800 --> 01:00:01.800
And here we are.

01:00:03.300 --> 01:00:04.470
Clarisse?

01:00:04.550 --> 01:00:05.600
Monsieur!

01:00:05.810 --> 01:00:08.140
I have come to take you away!
Fujiko, rope!

01:00:08.520 --> 01:00:10.020
Don't order me around!

01:00:17.650 --> 01:00:18.610
Miss Fujiko!

01:00:20.450 --> 01:00:21.490
Go, quick!

01:00:34.830 --> 01:00:36.710
-Monsieur!
-OK, you're safe now.

01:00:42.300 --> 01:00:44.050
Pops, over here! Here, here, here!

01:00:44.430 --> 01:00:47.350
Like it's that easy, you blithering idiot!

01:00:52.390 --> 01:00:53.850
All right, that's good!

01:01:16.960 --> 01:01:17.880
Lupin!

01:01:20.250 --> 01:01:22.220
Don't move, you she-rat!

01:01:26.470 --> 01:01:30.350
Fujiko, I have a lot of questions
to put to you later.

01:01:30.430 --> 01:01:33.140
-Jodot, finish Lupin.
-Yes, sir.

01:01:33.310 --> 01:01:34.600
No! You mustn't shoot him!

01:01:34.850 --> 01:01:37.110
If you mean to kill him,
then I will die, too!

01:01:37.690 --> 01:01:38.650
Fire.

01:01:58.580 --> 01:02:01.380
Your attitude is commendable, Clarisse.

01:02:05.840 --> 01:02:07.890
Get the ring back and come here.

01:02:08.850 --> 01:02:11.470
If you become my wife,
I'll spare Lupin's life.

01:02:12.720 --> 01:02:14.560
Or you can both die now.

01:02:15.230 --> 01:02:16.810
I'll let you choose as you will.

01:02:27.530 --> 01:02:29.320
Monsieur, the ring...

01:02:30.160 --> 01:02:32.240
No, Clarisse.

01:02:32.580 --> 01:02:33.620
You can't...

01:02:34.120 --> 01:02:36.660
Under his collar.
Lupin always hides things there.

01:02:37.460 --> 01:02:39.920
Damn you, Fujiko...

01:02:52.760 --> 01:02:53.680
Here is the ring.

01:02:53.770 --> 01:02:57.520
Spare this man and Miss Fujiko, or else
I will simply throw it in the lake.

01:02:57.850 --> 01:03:01.690
Trust me. Put it on your finger
and come over here.

01:03:01.770 --> 01:03:02.770
Shall I fire?

01:03:02.860 --> 01:03:04.360
Wait until the ring gets here.

01:03:14.490 --> 01:03:15.500
Lupin!

01:03:19.830 --> 01:03:21.080
Shoot them! Don't let them get away!

01:03:26.340 --> 01:03:28.510
You dirty coward!
You said you would spare them!

01:03:29.630 --> 01:03:33.100
They'd seen the basement workshop.
You thought I'd let them leave alive?

01:03:39.940 --> 01:03:41.940
I finally have it in my hands!

01:03:58.080 --> 01:04:00.620
Lupin, we'll say you owe me one for today.

01:04:00.710 --> 01:04:01.540
Later.

01:04:08.590 --> 01:04:10.760
And now,
we retreat without seeing any action?

01:04:15.560 --> 01:04:17.390
We can't go much longer!

01:04:17.470 --> 01:04:18.680
Jump down!

01:04:31.570 --> 01:04:33.870
Yet another worthless object
to fall prey to my blade.

01:04:35.910 --> 01:04:39.250
Lupin, you better not kick the bucket
before I catch you!

01:04:42.920 --> 01:04:45.250
Whatever the case,
this is certainly a problem.

01:04:45.330 --> 01:04:46.790
A dark plot is what this is.

01:04:50.670 --> 01:04:52.510
Please order me to move against them!

01:04:52.590 --> 01:04:54.760
We have all this indisputable evidence!

01:04:54.840 --> 01:04:56.050
I saw it myself!

01:04:56.140 --> 01:04:58.430
A whole row of
state-of-the-art printing presses...

01:04:58.510 --> 01:05:00.310
I know that!

01:05:02.230 --> 01:05:04.850
This is a highly political problem.

01:05:04.940 --> 01:05:08.440
Our jurisdiction here at Interpol
is limited to international crimes.

01:05:08.820 --> 01:05:11.570
Secretary General,
it is clear that this is criminal!

01:05:11.650 --> 01:05:12.950
You just don't get it.

01:05:13.320 --> 01:05:15.620
We're talking about a sovereign state
and a member of the UN.

01:05:15.700 --> 01:05:18.530
Even Interpol cannot conduct
a compulsory investigation.

01:05:18.910 --> 01:05:21.540
Not only that, but the situation
is exceedingly unfavorable for us.

01:05:21.620 --> 01:05:22.790
Did you see this photo

01:05:22.870 --> 01:05:25.750
that's on the front page
of every newspaper around the world?

01:05:25.960 --> 01:05:29.000
The bravery of the Count,
who personally protected his bride.

01:05:29.090 --> 01:05:31.340
"Lupin Fails to Abduct Princess Clarisse".

01:05:31.550 --> 01:05:34.630
They also say, "Lupin's Accomplice
Disguised As Zenigata".

01:05:34.720 --> 01:05:36.340
That was all me, the real McCoy.

01:05:36.800 --> 01:05:37.800
That's problematic.

01:05:37.890 --> 01:05:39.890
As an active duty police officer,
that was imprudent of you.

01:05:40.180 --> 01:05:42.520
I believe I reported what really happened!

01:05:43.060 --> 01:05:46.520
The issue here is,
which side the public will believe.

01:05:46.600 --> 01:05:47.770
We stand no chance, surely.

01:05:48.270 --> 01:05:51.650
The Count supposedly has a lot
of political friends in the West.

01:05:51.730 --> 01:05:54.740
I imagine many countries would have
a problem if the truth were revealed.

01:05:54.990 --> 01:05:57.450
Exactly! In point of fact,
there's proof that a certain country

01:05:57.530 --> 01:05:59.580
ordered a massive quantity
of counterfeit U.S. dollar bills!

01:06:00.160 --> 01:06:02.790
And these fake rubles
weren't ordered by your CIA?

01:06:02.870 --> 01:06:04.160
-What? How dare you?
-Stop this!

01:06:04.250 --> 01:06:07.000
You can't be bringing up
international disputes here!

01:06:07.080 --> 01:06:09.380
Precisely! We have no choice
but to have each country

01:06:09.460 --> 01:06:11.670
come up with their own countermeasures
for the Gothic bills.

01:06:18.300 --> 01:06:20.550
Inspector, we are prepared to mobilize.

01:06:20.640 --> 01:06:23.350
We can depart for the Principality
of Cagliostro at any time.

01:06:24.810 --> 01:06:26.350
-We won't be mobilizing.
-Sir?

01:06:26.440 --> 01:06:30.560
We'll be off the Lupin case as soon
as they find someone to replace us.

01:06:31.190 --> 01:06:33.440
Everyone, prepare to return to Japan.

01:06:43.910 --> 01:06:45.040
It's me.

01:06:46.460 --> 01:06:47.420
Here's some food.

01:06:47.500 --> 01:06:48.620
Much appreciated.

01:06:48.710 --> 01:06:49.750
How is he?

01:06:49.920 --> 01:06:51.710
His fever seems to have gone down.

01:06:52.290 --> 01:06:54.420
It's thanks to you operating on him.

01:06:54.510 --> 01:06:56.630
If you want to thank someone,
thank that dog.

01:06:57.340 --> 01:07:01.600
That old dog is friendly to no one,
but he won't budge from that man's side.

01:07:01.930 --> 01:07:05.470
Otherwise, I probably wouldn't
have offered you folks shelter.

01:07:15.650 --> 01:07:17.070
Hey, Karl.

01:07:17.280 --> 01:07:18.610
He's awake!

01:07:19.490 --> 01:07:21.120
Lupin, how're your wounds?

01:07:23.530 --> 01:07:26.370
Jigen. Goemon. Long time no see.

01:07:26.790 --> 01:07:29.170
Long time? What're you saying?

01:07:29.250 --> 01:07:31.790
His memory is in temporary disarray
due to his injuries.

01:07:32.250 --> 01:07:35.800
Karl, you're not with your mistress today?

01:07:37.420 --> 01:07:40.260
How do you know that dog's name?

01:07:40.970 --> 01:07:43.180
Other than myself,
the only one left to know him as Karl

01:07:43.260 --> 01:07:44.760
should be the Lady Clarisse.

01:07:45.350 --> 01:07:46.470
Clarisse?

01:07:47.310 --> 01:07:51.230
I see,
so your mistress's name is Clarisse...

01:07:52.060 --> 01:07:53.230
Clarisse...

01:07:57.530 --> 01:07:58.490
Lupin.

01:07:59.030 --> 01:08:00.490
Jigen, what day is today?

01:08:00.610 --> 01:08:01.950
How many days has it been?

01:08:02.910 --> 01:08:04.080
Three days.

01:08:04.370 --> 01:08:06.870
What? Then the ceremony's tomorrow.

01:08:06.950 --> 01:08:08.250
No time to be...

01:08:10.330 --> 01:08:12.830
Come on, don't push it.
You'll reopen your wounds.

01:08:13.130 --> 01:08:15.750
Food. Bring me food.

01:08:16.090 --> 01:08:17.800
Food? Like rice porridge?

01:08:18.050 --> 01:08:21.220
I'm low on blood. Bring me whatever.
Just keep it coming.

01:08:21.840 --> 01:08:23.890
Easy for you to say, but...

01:08:23.970 --> 01:08:25.390
I'll handle it.

01:08:31.230 --> 01:08:33.310
You idiot,
quit stuffing yourself like that.

01:08:33.400 --> 01:08:35.020
Your stomach won't take it.

01:08:35.820 --> 01:08:38.730
Shut up! Even a jet airplane
can get fixed up in twelve hours!

01:08:50.960 --> 01:08:52.870
See? What'd I tell you? Need a wash basin?

01:08:55.040 --> 01:08:56.340
What's that?

01:08:59.090 --> 01:09:00.670
Says he'll sleep, now that he's eaten.

01:09:04.220 --> 01:09:05.640
I had no idea.

01:09:05.760 --> 01:09:07.390
All for the Lady Clarisse...

01:09:07.470 --> 01:09:10.310
But with Lupin in this shape...

01:09:10.390 --> 01:09:13.440
It sounds as though you have a great deal
of history with the Lady Clarisse.

01:09:14.190 --> 01:09:16.610
I used to be the palace groundskeeper.

01:09:17.230 --> 01:09:20.030
The Lady Clarisse loved plants as a child.

01:09:20.360 --> 01:09:24.280
When the Prince and his wife passed away
and she was to enter the convent,

01:09:24.360 --> 01:09:26.740
she entrusted this dog to me.

01:09:26.820 --> 01:09:31.290
So, he sniffed out
the Princess's scent on Lupin.

01:09:31.950 --> 01:09:35.120
How did this man know the dog's name?

01:09:35.500 --> 01:09:38.840
Who knows? This guy's
constantly falling in love, so...

01:09:38.920 --> 01:09:40.130
It's nothing like that.

01:09:40.210 --> 01:09:41.340
You were awake?

01:09:42.970 --> 01:09:45.300
It was over 10 years ago now.

01:09:46.340 --> 01:09:50.470
I was a greenhorn, eager to set out
and make a name for myself.

01:09:58.900 --> 01:10:00.520
<i>I did crazy things,</i>

01:10:00.650 --> 01:10:04.570
<i>and after making a real show of myself,</i>
<i>in the end,</i> <i>I went after the Gothic bills.</i>

01:10:13.870 --> 01:10:16.290
<i>I managed to pull myself up</i>
<i>onto the shore somehow,</i>

01:10:16.370 --> 01:10:18.380
<i>but I couldn't budge another inch.</i>

01:10:23.510 --> 01:10:25.550
Karl? What's wrong, Karl?

01:10:34.980 --> 01:10:38.150
<i>Looks like my time's come</i>
<i>to pay the piper.</i>

01:10:43.360 --> 01:10:44.360
Water...

01:10:56.830 --> 01:10:59.080
She helped me drink the water,
her hands shaking...

01:10:59.170 --> 01:11:02.800
And shining on her finger was that ring.

01:11:03.920 --> 01:11:05.550
I'm ashamed to say,

01:11:05.630 --> 01:11:08.260
I'd totally forgotten about it
until I saw the ring again.

01:11:16.680 --> 01:11:18.140
That's Fujiko's motorbike.

01:11:18.980 --> 01:11:20.600
It's a clipping from today's newspaper.

01:11:20.770 --> 01:11:22.230
It says that tomorrow morning,

01:11:22.310 --> 01:11:24.820
an archbishop is coming
from the Vatican for the ceremony.

01:11:36.250 --> 01:11:37.910
I'm quitting!

01:11:38.620 --> 01:11:39.620
Fujiko?

01:11:40.370 --> 01:11:42.960
What? Lupin's going to hit
the wedding? Is this true?

01:11:43.500 --> 01:11:45.000
If you're pursuing Lupin,

01:11:45.090 --> 01:11:46.880
you have full authority
to mobilize, right?

01:11:48.220 --> 01:11:50.550
Right... I hadn't thought of that!

01:12:14.240 --> 01:12:16.240
We're in a hurry! Would you move aside?

01:12:16.330 --> 01:12:19.620
It's no use.
It's completely jammed up ahead.

01:12:19.710 --> 01:12:22.000
They said there was a landslide
seven kilos down the road.

01:12:22.080 --> 01:12:24.130
Is there no other way?

01:12:24.210 --> 01:12:26.920
-We're going to be late.
-Right...

01:12:27.000 --> 01:12:29.840
By gosh,
aren't ya the fine Lord Archbishop?

01:12:30.420 --> 01:12:32.630
Yep, just like I reckoned.

01:12:32.720 --> 01:12:35.720
Would you be so kind
as to bless this little baby goat?

01:12:37.680 --> 01:12:39.390
You're a local, right?

01:12:39.480 --> 01:12:42.230
Aren't there any other ways
to get to the Castle of Cagliostro?

01:12:42.310 --> 01:12:44.440
If ya don't mind country roads,
there's a way over there.

01:12:44.650 --> 01:12:45.730
Thank goodness!

01:12:45.810 --> 01:12:46.860
Would you show me the way?

01:12:46.940 --> 01:12:48.150
Come on, get in. Get in.

01:12:48.400 --> 01:12:52.320
Sure, sure. If it's for the fine
Lord Archbishop, then sure.

01:12:58.330 --> 01:12:59.290
Keep it up, men!

01:12:59.370 --> 01:13:01.000
One more hill and we'll be at the border!

01:13:01.080 --> 01:13:03.290
We have to get there
by dusk at the latest!

01:13:05.500 --> 01:13:07.540
Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

01:13:16.600 --> 01:13:18.010
Is this really all right?

01:13:18.310 --> 01:13:20.100
Publicizing this on TV...

01:13:20.520 --> 01:13:25.730
His Highness wishes to show the world
that this is a legitimate wedding.

01:13:25.810 --> 01:13:29.400
His Grace, the Archbishop, has arrived.

01:13:36.200 --> 01:13:37.990
Do you think Lupin will show up?

01:13:38.280 --> 01:13:40.990
My Shadows will guard the bride.

01:13:41.290 --> 01:13:43.540
All your men have to do is guard the gate!

01:13:43.620 --> 01:13:44.620
Yes, sir.

01:14:46.100 --> 01:14:49.060
The time has come for light and shadow
to become as one.

01:14:49.610 --> 01:14:51.650
Come, Clarisse.

01:16:18.610 --> 01:16:21.030
The House of Cagliostro
is a noble family of ancient blood.

01:16:21.110 --> 01:16:26.370
Bring here the proof
that you are their rightful heirs.

01:16:32.460 --> 01:16:35.000
In accordance with the customs of old,

01:16:35.090 --> 01:16:38.420
the exchange of rings
shall constitute your marriage vows.

01:16:39.170 --> 01:16:41.630
Daughter of the Prince of the Principality
of Cagliostro,

01:16:42.430 --> 01:16:47.930
Clarisse de Cagliostro,
do you consent to this marriage?

01:16:48.020 --> 01:16:51.270
If you do not object,
then respond with silence.

01:17:10.160 --> 01:17:12.710
May God bless you...

01:17:13.120 --> 01:17:13.960
I object.

01:17:16.540 --> 01:17:20.380
These marriage rites
are profoundly tainted by greed.

01:17:34.060 --> 01:17:35.020
This is a curse!

01:17:35.100 --> 01:17:36.230
No need to fuss.

01:17:36.310 --> 01:17:38.400
So, that accursed rat has appeared.

01:17:56.210 --> 01:18:00.500
I have come to speak on behalf of the dead
in the dungeon underground.

01:18:00.590 --> 01:18:02.710
I want the bride.

01:18:03.340 --> 01:18:04.880
We cannot carry out the ceremony now.

01:18:04.970 --> 01:18:07.180
Get back.
This will be a fine bit of entertainment.

01:18:09.050 --> 01:18:12.720
Clarisse, I've come for you.

01:18:17.730 --> 01:18:19.150
It's a monster!

01:18:19.270 --> 01:18:20.940
Something incredible has happened!

01:18:21.020 --> 01:18:22.860
It's Lupin! Lupin's appeared!

01:18:22.940 --> 01:18:24.190
Stop the broadcast!

01:18:24.320 --> 01:18:25.780
What are you doing?

01:18:26.240 --> 01:18:27.070
Please wait one moment. Move out!

01:18:30.280 --> 01:18:32.830
Clarisse. Clarisse.

01:18:33.450 --> 01:18:35.910
Poor thing.
You've been drugged, haven't you?

01:18:36.000 --> 01:18:39.170
Curse you, Count. You made it
so she couldn't speak, didn't you?

01:18:48.180 --> 01:18:52.260
-Monsieur!
-You mustn't. You mustn't get closer.

01:18:53.060 --> 01:18:54.430
That was foolish, Lupin!

01:18:54.520 --> 01:18:56.060
Take care of those men as well!

01:18:58.600 --> 01:18:59.560
Clarisse.

01:18:59.650 --> 01:19:01.270
Don't cry, Clarisse.

01:19:03.480 --> 01:19:05.860
I'll come to you now.

01:19:13.410 --> 01:19:14.620
What's going on here?

01:19:14.700 --> 01:19:17.580
I wonder if this gift
will be to your liking, Count.

01:19:17.660 --> 01:19:18.670
Highness!

01:19:19.080 --> 01:19:21.290
They're the counterfeit bills you printed.

01:19:21.380 --> 01:19:23.380
Take them as payment for the rings.

01:19:24.460 --> 01:19:25.380
Blast it!

01:19:25.460 --> 01:19:28.090
Find him! He has to be in here somewhere!

01:19:30.180 --> 01:19:31.470
I've definitely got them now.

01:19:31.850 --> 01:19:32.680
You're...

01:19:33.430 --> 01:19:34.430
Lupin!

01:19:34.770 --> 01:19:36.270
Monsieur!

01:19:36.680 --> 01:19:38.850
Curse you! Play me for a fool, will you?

01:19:38.940 --> 01:19:40.020
No burning up with jealousy now.

01:19:40.100 --> 01:19:42.650
Or you'll get burned, Lolita-loving Count.

01:19:54.530 --> 01:19:55.490
Take that!

01:20:09.010 --> 01:20:10.470
Lupin! Lupin! Lupin!

01:20:10.590 --> 01:20:12.930
Take that! Ladies and gentlemen,
pardon me for keeping you waiting.

01:20:13.010 --> 01:20:14.050
We will now resume our broadcast.

01:20:14.470 --> 01:20:16.470
The wedding hall is now in utter chaos!

01:20:17.640 --> 01:20:19.390
-Well, then... Buh-bye!
-Die!

01:20:27.110 --> 01:20:28.610
After him! Don't let him get away!

01:20:29.240 --> 01:20:32.570
Lupin has fled! The Count is in a rage
and hot on his heels!

01:20:33.280 --> 01:20:35.080
The police have come storming in!

01:20:36.830 --> 01:20:38.540
Lupin is under the altar!

01:20:39.250 --> 01:20:41.410
Make a hole! Attack!

01:20:43.170 --> 01:20:45.880
Zenigata's men are pushing hard
towards the altar!

01:20:46.040 --> 01:20:48.170
Here's the gendarmerie! In the lead is...

01:20:48.630 --> 01:20:49.840
Gendarme Captain Gustav!

01:20:49.920 --> 01:20:51.380
Secure our rear!

01:20:53.220 --> 01:20:54.220
Why you!

01:20:55.930 --> 01:20:58.720
Give no quarter! Justice is on our side!

01:20:59.430 --> 01:21:01.520
The fighting is truly fierce!

01:21:01.600 --> 01:21:03.900
What could possibly be beneath the altar?

01:21:04.690 --> 01:21:07.360
It's a staircase!
There's a hole leading underground!

01:21:07.900 --> 01:21:09.860
Could Lupin be inside that hole?

01:21:09.940 --> 01:21:11.900
Let us follow with the camera!

01:21:12.700 --> 01:21:14.360
Darn you, Lupin!

01:21:15.910 --> 01:21:17.080
Lupin! Lupin!

01:21:17.160 --> 01:21:18.700
That idiot! What's he doing?

01:21:19.160 --> 01:21:21.200
He's ignoring his orders! Call him off!

01:21:21.290 --> 01:21:23.370
This is being broadcast via satellite!
It's too late!

01:21:24.620 --> 01:21:26.210
What the heck is this place?

01:21:26.840 --> 01:21:29.130
This practically looks like
a national minting facility!

01:21:29.670 --> 01:21:31.130
What's that over there?

01:21:33.470 --> 01:21:35.340
<i>Oh, wow! These are Japanese bills!</i>

01:21:35.430 --> 01:21:36.680
<i>Counterfeit bills!</i>

01:21:36.930 --> 01:21:39.100
Talk about hamming it up...

01:21:39.180 --> 01:21:41.770
<i>-This is an incredible revelation!</i>
<i>-Take a look!</i>

01:21:41.850 --> 01:21:43.690
<i>They're counterfeit currency</i>
<i>from all over the world!</i>

01:21:43.770 --> 01:21:46.610
<i>I've made a terrible discovery</i>
<i>during my pursuit of Lupin!</i>

01:21:46.690 --> 01:21:47.560
<i>What should I do?</i>

01:22:00.490 --> 01:22:02.200
First things first,
we're getting out of this castle.

01:22:02.290 --> 01:22:03.710
I'm counting on you, Jigen. Goemon.

01:22:03.790 --> 01:22:05.540
Leave it to us. We'll hold them off here.

01:22:05.620 --> 01:22:06.500
Come on.

01:22:11.250 --> 01:22:12.130
Gentlemen.

01:22:12.510 --> 01:22:15.050
I beg of you to be careful.
And you, too, Noble Jigen.

01:22:16.130 --> 01:22:17.720
Please make certain
that you return safely.

01:22:18.140 --> 01:22:19.680
I will never forget
this debt of gratitude.

01:22:20.510 --> 01:22:21.640
Now, you must go.

01:22:24.100 --> 01:22:25.980
Clarisse, hurry.

01:22:26.060 --> 01:22:27.020
Coming.

01:22:33.110 --> 01:22:34.950
She called me Noble Jigen.

01:22:35.240 --> 01:22:36.240
A lovely lady...

01:22:41.870 --> 01:22:43.290
Let's get this started!

01:22:51.210 --> 01:22:53.590
There is an extra keenness
to my steel cleaver this evening.

01:22:54.050 --> 01:22:56.470
Curse you, Lupin, this isn't over yet!

01:22:59.180 --> 01:23:01.180
Leave matters within
the castle to me, sir.

01:23:20.200 --> 01:23:22.620
-Are your wounds causing you pain?
-Nah, they're nothing.

01:23:22.700 --> 01:23:24.200
Now, let's get over this thing.

01:23:30.710 --> 01:23:32.840
Two goats facing each other...

01:23:38.840 --> 01:23:40.800
There are Gothic letters
carved along the seam.

01:23:41.090 --> 01:23:43.760
"Binding light and shadow..."

01:23:43.970 --> 01:23:46.350
They're worn down and hard to read.

01:23:46.430 --> 01:23:50.100
"Binding light and shadow,
tolling the hours is the goat on high,

01:23:50.190 --> 01:23:53.360
into whose eyes,
facing the sun, I bid you place me."

01:23:54.270 --> 01:23:57.070
Those words have been passed down
in my family since ancient times.

01:23:57.150 --> 01:23:58.400
Does that help?

01:23:58.950 --> 01:24:01.910
Yes, it helps!
Now I know the answer to the riddle!

01:24:03.700 --> 01:24:05.370
It's the Count. Come, this way.

01:24:11.290 --> 01:24:13.960
They're going inside the machine room
of the clock tower! Moor the boat!

01:24:28.890 --> 01:24:29.890
There!

01:24:30.480 --> 01:24:32.100
Here they come.

01:24:36.440 --> 01:24:37.900
Hot, hot, hot, hot, hot, hot!

01:24:39.030 --> 01:24:40.110
Well, that's no good.

01:24:41.450 --> 01:24:42.740
Shut down the lasers.

01:24:42.820 --> 01:24:45.280
The idiot. Does he think they
can get out of here?

01:25:04.090 --> 01:25:05.470
-Scared?
-No.

01:25:05.550 --> 01:25:06.510
Fantastic!

01:25:06.600 --> 01:25:07.680
Here we go!

01:25:11.890 --> 01:25:13.020
Don't let him get away!

01:25:30.450 --> 01:25:31.290
Don't look!

01:25:34.250 --> 01:25:35.330
We can't go this way.

01:25:35.420 --> 01:25:36.880
You men use the stairs!

01:25:36.960 --> 01:25:37.880
Yes, sir!

01:25:44.800 --> 01:25:45.800
Stay here.

01:25:45.930 --> 01:25:47.510
-I'm going to block the entrance.
-Be careful!

01:25:47.600 --> 01:25:48.970
I'll be right back!

01:26:00.730 --> 01:26:01.860
There!

01:26:23.300 --> 01:26:25.130
Monsieur! Behind you!

01:26:30.600 --> 01:26:32.390
Hey, there, Count!

01:26:32.890 --> 01:26:35.560
Accursed rat! I'll run you through!

01:26:35.730 --> 01:26:37.900
Looks like we've come
to the finale at last, Count.

01:27:04.710 --> 01:27:06.630
And one more!

01:27:14.060 --> 01:27:18.350
Hey, Count C, I dare you to come get me!

01:27:26.650 --> 01:27:27.900
Monsieur!

01:27:35.910 --> 01:27:38.160
I'll start by taking care of you first!

01:27:38.460 --> 01:27:39.960
Clarisse, run!

01:27:40.580 --> 01:27:41.750
I'm coming!

01:28:08.700 --> 01:28:10.360
How far do you think you're going?

01:28:10.990 --> 01:28:12.280
Clarisse...

01:28:18.540 --> 01:28:21.790
Come on, come on. What's wrong?

01:28:22.460 --> 01:28:24.130
Not running anymore?

01:28:25.340 --> 01:28:28.010
This will be the end
of the Cagliostro bloodline.

01:28:28.090 --> 01:28:29.090
Die, Clarisse.

01:28:29.170 --> 01:28:30.260
Wait, Count!

01:28:30.340 --> 01:28:31.630
Let's make a deal!

01:28:32.090 --> 01:28:35.140
It's too late!
You can watch this woman die!

01:28:35.220 --> 01:28:36.510
Listen to what I've got to say.

01:28:37.600 --> 01:28:39.890
I'll tell you the secret to these rings.

01:28:39.980 --> 01:28:42.690
You can do whatever you want
with the treasure.

01:28:42.810 --> 01:28:45.400
But give up on the girl. Let her go free.

01:28:46.150 --> 01:28:48.610
Look at the Capricorn on the clock face.

01:28:48.990 --> 01:28:51.700
That's the goat that faces the sun
and tolls the hours.

01:28:52.030 --> 01:28:54.530
It's got two holes in its eyes
to fit the rings into.

01:28:55.450 --> 01:28:57.290
I'll let you have these rings,

01:28:57.370 --> 01:29:01.370
but if you kill her, I'll throw them
in the lake and I'll kill you.

01:29:30.740 --> 01:29:32.320
That's far enough.

01:29:32.400 --> 01:29:33.990
Let Clarisse go inside.

01:29:34.740 --> 01:29:36.620
All right, fine.

01:29:43.830 --> 01:29:47.710
Lupin, you have to save your trump cards
for the end.

01:29:49.340 --> 01:29:50.340
Come!

01:29:54.880 --> 01:29:57.640
These are definitely the genuine articles.
The rings are mine now.

01:29:58.010 --> 01:30:00.470
Here's your payment
for solving the riddle.

01:30:04.980 --> 01:30:06.190
Let go!

01:30:06.900 --> 01:30:08.150
Clarisse!

01:30:11.360 --> 01:30:12.190
Let go!

01:31:42.910 --> 01:31:43.870
The clock tower!

01:31:55.550 --> 01:31:56.420
Your Highness...

01:32:32.920 --> 01:32:34.040
What the heck is that?

01:33:01.360 --> 01:33:03.950
Cagliostro is done for.

01:33:04.870 --> 01:33:05.870
Cut me down.

01:33:06.450 --> 01:33:08.370
I will not kill needlessly.

01:33:58.040 --> 01:34:00.250
-Monsieur...
-Hey, can you stand?

01:34:00.340 --> 01:34:01.420
Take a look.

01:34:24.900 --> 01:34:26.860
The hidden treasure...

01:34:27.780 --> 01:34:30.950
I had no idea there was
a Roman city beneath the lake.

01:34:32.240 --> 01:34:34.290
When the Romans
were driven from this land,

01:34:34.370 --> 01:34:36.460
they built that floodgate
and submerged it.

01:34:36.540 --> 01:34:39.420
And your ancestors quietly inherited it.

01:34:49.350 --> 01:34:52.060
Truly, a treasure for all mankind.

01:34:52.140 --> 01:34:54.430
It's too big for my pocket.

01:35:12.870 --> 01:35:15.290
So, Interpol got their lazy bums
into gear.

01:35:30.550 --> 01:35:31.970
Will you be leaving?

01:35:33.350 --> 01:35:34.350
Yeah.

01:35:34.430 --> 01:35:37.350
A lot of scary men just showed up, so...

01:35:39.940 --> 01:35:41.480
Take me with you.

01:35:41.560 --> 01:35:43.770
I can't work as a thief yet,
but I'll learn, I promise!

01:35:44.150 --> 01:35:46.070
I... I...

01:35:46.990 --> 01:35:47.860
Please!

01:35:48.320 --> 01:35:49.700
I want to go with you.

01:35:52.870 --> 01:35:53.870
Clarisse.

01:36:03.540 --> 01:36:05.420
Don't give me that silly talk.

01:36:05.750 --> 01:36:07.840
You want to go back
into the darkness again?

01:36:07.920 --> 01:36:10.220
It's taken you this long
to get into the sun.

01:36:10.590 --> 01:36:13.680
Right? Your life is
only getting started here.

01:36:14.220 --> 01:36:16.600
You can't become all grubby like me.

01:36:17.140 --> 01:36:18.020
Oh, yeah!

01:36:18.100 --> 01:36:19.940
If you ever run into any trouble,
just call any time, OK?

01:36:20.020 --> 01:36:23.520
Monsieur will come running, even if
it's from the other side of the globe.

01:36:33.450 --> 01:36:34.740
Karl!

01:36:36.200 --> 01:36:38.000
Karl! Karl!

01:36:38.080 --> 01:36:39.080
Lady Clarisse.

01:36:39.160 --> 01:36:40.250
Grandpa!

01:36:50.670 --> 01:36:52.430
-Monsieur!
-Toodle-oo!

01:36:53.550 --> 01:36:55.220
Princess!

01:36:57.560 --> 01:36:58.770
Monsieur!

01:36:59.270 --> 01:37:01.230
Clarisse, take care!

01:37:01.690 --> 01:37:02.850
Goodbye!

01:37:05.560 --> 01:37:08.900
Thank you, everyone! Goodbye!

01:37:09.190 --> 01:37:10.440
Goodbye!

01:37:10.530 --> 01:37:12.860
Goodbye!

01:37:25.210 --> 01:37:27.460
Dang it! One step too late!

01:37:27.550 --> 01:37:29.170
That darn Lupin got away with his loot!

01:37:29.710 --> 01:37:32.130
No, that man took nothing.

01:37:32.420 --> 01:37:34.430
He honored me by fighting for my sake.

01:37:34.840 --> 01:37:37.930
No, ma'am,
he ran off with a tremendous prize.

01:37:39.640 --> 01:37:40.850
Your heart.

01:37:43.270 --> 01:37:44.140
Yes.

01:37:45.270 --> 01:37:46.690
Well, then, please excuse me!

01:37:52.030 --> 01:37:54.780
After Lupin! We follow him
to the ends of the Earth!

01:37:55.200 --> 01:37:57.030
SAITAMA PREFECTURAL POLICE

01:38:14.590 --> 01:38:17.390
What a refreshing bunch
of fellows they were.

01:38:17.680 --> 01:38:21.720
I feel as though I have known
that gentleman since a long time ago.

01:38:22.890 --> 01:38:23.890
Lupin...

01:38:23.980 --> 01:38:25.940
I'm sure... I'm sure we'll meet again.

01:38:31.360 --> 01:38:33.820
She was a nice girl, wasn't she?

01:38:35.990 --> 01:38:38.490
You could stay behind, you know.

01:38:41.950 --> 01:38:43.450
Fujicakes!

01:38:43.540 --> 01:38:45.960
Lupin, take a look at what I scored!

01:38:46.540 --> 01:38:48.830
Those are the master printing plates
for the counterfeit bills!

01:38:49.130 --> 01:38:52.050
-Wow! I'd love to be your friend!
-So long!

01:38:53.340 --> 01:38:56.430
Hey! Hold on a second there!

01:38:59.300 --> 01:39:01.600
Crap, here comes Pops again.

01:39:02.140 --> 01:39:04.310
Lupin, you won't get away this time!

01:39:24.040 --> 01:39:29.540
THE END
